            <title>[LU-21053] lctl: set_param -P of a renamed parameter returns 0, but the setting is lost after a remount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21053</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A site that used `lctl set_param -P` with a parameter name from 2.16&lt;br/&gt;
loses the setting after an upgrade, with no message. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8066" title="Move lustre procfs handling to sysfs and debugfs." class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-8066"&gt;LU-8066&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
(commit 43e1ae99ff) moved the mdc parameters `mdc_lsom` and&lt;br/&gt;
`mdc_dom_min_repsize` to sysfs as `lsom` and `dom_min_repsize`.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. On a master (2.17.55 or newer) client, run&lt;br/&gt;
   `lctl set_param -P mdc.*.mdc_lsom=Off` and&lt;br/&gt;
   `lctl set_param -P mdc.*.mdc_dom_min_repsize=4096`. These two names are the&lt;br/&gt;
   2.16 names.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Remount the client.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Read the parameters under their new names.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Result: `set_param -P` returns 0. After the remount, the settings do&lt;br/&gt;
not apply, and the console shows no message. The control parameter&lt;br/&gt;
`max_rpcs_in_flight=16` keeps its name, and it applies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected result: the old name applies under the new name, and lctl&lt;br/&gt;
prints one warning for each renamed parameter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both `set_param -P` paths end in the userspace command `lctl&lt;br/&gt;
set_param`. The udev rule runs it, and the upcall runs it. lctl already has a&lt;br/&gt;
table of deprecated parameters in `setparam_check_deprecated()`. A&lt;br/&gt;
rename map there covers both paths with no kernel change. The kernel&lt;br/&gt;
rename table `cfg_interop_param` covers only `conf_param` records.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tested on 1 VM node: the loss occurs without a fix. With a 56-line&lt;br/&gt;
prototype rename map, both 2.16 names apply after the remount.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
